{
  "id": "cb6",
  "title": "Groups and Levels",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "cb6-l1",
      "title": "Group Items",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "Data comes in records: a customer has a name, a city and a number. In COBOL, an 01 without a PIC is a group, and the fields under it get higher level numbers like 05.",
        "The group is all of its fields, one after the other. DISPLAY CUSTOMER shows them all together, exactly as they sit in memory.",
        "MOVE SPACES TO CUSTOMER clears the whole record at once. Levels can go deeper: 10 under 05, up to 49."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.",
          "       PROGRAM-ID. RECORD.",
          "       DATA DIVISION.",
          "       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.",
          "       01 CUSTOMER.",
          "          05 CUST-NAME  PIC X(6).",
          "          05 CUST-CITY  PIC X(8).",
          "          05 CUST-BORN  PIC 9(4).",
          "       PROCEDURE DIVISION.",
          "           MOVE \"GRACE\" TO CUST-NAME.",
          "           MOVE \"NEW YORK\" TO CUST-CITY.",
          "           MOVE 1906 TO CUST-BORN.",
          "           DISPLAY \"[\" CUSTOMER \"]\".",
          "           DISPLAY \"CITY: \" CUST-CITY.",
          "           MOVE SPACES TO CUSTOMER.",
          "           DISPLAY \"[\" CUSTOMER \"]\".",
          "           STOP RUN."
        ],
        "output": [
          "[GRACE NEW YORK1906]",
          "CITY: NEW YORK",
          "[                  ]"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "cb6-l1-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What is an 01 level without a PIC?",
          "options": [
            "A group: it's made of the fields below it",
            "An error",
            "A text field of 1 character",
            "A comment"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Only the elementary fields at the bottom have a PIC."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb6-l1-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does this job show?",
          "code": [
            "       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.",
            "       PROGRAM-ID. GROUP.",
            "       DATA DIVISION.",
            "       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.",
            "       01 PERSON.",
            "          05 NAME-PART PIC X(3).",
            "          05 YEAR-PART PIC 9(4).",
            "       PROCEDURE DIVISION.",
            "           MOVE \"ADA\" TO NAME-PART.",
            "           MOVE 1815 TO YEAR-PART.",
            "           DISPLAY \"[\" PERSON \"]\".",
            "           STOP RUN."
          ],
          "options": [
            "[ADA1815]",
            "[ADA 1815]",
            "[ADA  1815]",
            "[1815ADA]"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "The group is NAME-PART (3 characters) followed by YEAR-PART."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb6-l1-e3",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "Clear the whole customer record.",
          "code": [
            "           MOVE ___ TO CUSTOMER."
          ],
          "options": [
            "SPACES",
            "ZERO",
            "NOTHING",
            "NULL"
          ],
          "answer": "SPACES",
          "explanation": "SPACES fills every character of the group."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb6-l1-e4",
          "type": "find_bug",
          "prompt": "This job doesn't compile. Which line is wrong?",
          "code": [
            "       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.",
            "       PROGRAM-ID. GRP.",
            "       DATA DIVISION.",
            "       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.",
            "       01 ORDER-REC PIC X(10).",
            "          05 ORDER-NO PIC 9(5).",
            "       PROCEDURE DIVISION.",
            "           STOP RUN."
          ],
          "answer": 4,
          "explanation": "ORDER-REC has a PIC, so it can't have fields under it. A group has no PIC."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb6-l1-e5",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "How long is a group with PIC X(6), PIC X(8) and PIC 9(4) under it?",
          "options": [
            "18 characters",
            "6",
            "3",
            "It has no length"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "6 + 8 + 4."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb6-l1-e6",
          "type": "order_lines",
          "prompt": "Put the record in order: a group with two fields.",
          "lines": [
            "       01 BOOK.",
            "          05 TITLE    PIC X(20).",
            "          05 PAGES    PIC 9(4)."
          ],
          "answer": [
            "       01 BOOK.",
            "          05 TITLE    PIC X(20).",
            "          05 PAGES    PIC 9(4)."
          ],
          "explanation": "The 01 group first, then its 05 fields."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cb6-l2",
      "title": "Report Lines",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "A printed report line is a group too: texts, spaces and edited fields side by side. FILLER is a field without a name, for parts you never change, like labels and gaps.",
        "Fill in the named fields, then DISPLAY the whole line. Everything lines up in columns by itself, because every field has a fixed size.",
        "This is how COBOL programs printed millions of bills and bank statements: one line layout, filled again for every row."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.",
          "       PROGRAM-ID. REPORT.",
          "       DATA DIVISION.",
          "       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.",
          "       01 REPORT-LINE.",
          "          05 RL-ITEM    PIC X(8).",
          "          05 FILLER     PIC X(2) VALUE SPACES.",
          "          05 RL-QTY     PIC ZZ9.",
          "          05 FILLER     PIC X(3) VALUE \" X \".",
          "          05 RL-PRICE   PIC $$$9.99.",
          "       PROCEDURE DIVISION.",
          "           MOVE \"COFFEE\" TO RL-ITEM.",
          "           MOVE 3 TO RL-QTY.",
          "           MOVE 7.5 TO RL-PRICE.",
          "           DISPLAY REPORT-LINE.",
          "           MOVE \"CAKE\" TO RL-ITEM.",
          "           MOVE 12 TO RL-QTY.",
          "           MOVE 23.75 TO RL-PRICE.",
          "           DISPLAY REPORT-LINE.",
          "           STOP RUN."
        ],
        "output": [
          "COFFEE      3 X   $7.50",
          "CAKE       12 X  $23.75"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "cb6-l2-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What is FILLER?",
          "options": [
            "A field without a name, for fixed parts like labels and gaps",
            "A field that fills up automatically",
            "A comment",
            "The last field of a group"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "You can't refer to it, so it keeps its VALUE."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb6-l2-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does this job show?",
          "code": [
            "       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.",
            "       PROGRAM-ID. LINE.",
            "       DATA DIVISION.",
            "       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.",
            "       01 LINE-OUT.",
            "          05 FILLER PIC X(7) VALUE \"TOTAL: \".",
            "          05 T-OUT  PIC ZZ9.",
            "       PROCEDURE DIVISION.",
            "           MOVE 42 TO T-OUT.",
            "           DISPLAY LINE-OUT.",
            "           STOP RUN."
          ],
          "options": [
            "TOTAL:  42",
            "TOTAL:42",
            "TOTAL: 042",
            "  42TOTAL:"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "The FILLER holds \"TOTAL: \", then the ZZ9 field shows \" 42\"."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb6-l2-e3",
          "type": "fill_blank",
